 "conclusion": "Neither slot count reaches the 2x target. Two slots lower the 4-session p95 by about 20% but raise its p50 by about 50% and cut throughput; four slots stay. On four cores the four-session cost is intrinsic (the decode batch is compute-bound), so the roadmap fallback applies: the single-session profile is documented and the recommended concurrency limit is 2 sessions (docs/decisions/002-nfr007-single-session-profile.md)."
